meta {
  name: Email unsubscribe (public)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/khatm/email/unsubscribe?token={{unsubscribeToken}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  token: signed JWT from the email link
}

docs {
  Replaces: the email-unsubscribe edge function. PUBLIC — no session; the
  token is the authorization. Response is a small HTML page (opened from an
  email client), not JSON.

  Token contract (currently supabase/functions/_shared/jwt.ts — signer and
  verifier live in ONE module; keep that in the port):
  - HS256, backend-owned secret
  - claims: sub = participant_id, iss = backend origin,
    aud = "email-unsubscribe", exp = 30 days
  - ALL failures (bad signature, expired, wrong iss/aud, missing sub) return
    the SAME "link expired" page — no oracle distinguishing why.

  Effect: sets email_notifications_enabled = false on that participant row.

  KNOWN PRODUCT CAVEAT (decide during port): the flag is per group-membership
  but the confirmation page implies a global unsubscribe — a user in several
  groups keeps receiving email from the others. If Hikmah wants global
  semantics, move the preference to the user profile and update the token to
  carry the user id. See HIKMAH-INTEGRATION.md §6.1.

  DB update failures still return the success page to the user (the link was
  valid; the failure is internal) but must be logged via Pino.
}
